      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Rancid Bloat",
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "curse",
        "disease",
        "divine"
      ],
      "text": "This disease and damage from it can't be healed unless this curse is removed. A creature killed by rancid bloat rots away to waterlogged pieces of flesh and can't be resurrected except by an 8th-rank Resurrect ritual or similar magic.\n\nSaving Throw DC 38 Fortitude save\n\nStage 1 carrier with no ill effect (1 minute)\n\nStage 2 12d6 void damage, Clumsy 2, and Enfeebled 2 (1 day)\n\nStage 3 16d6 void damage, Clumsy 4, and Enfeebled 4 (1 day)"
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Whirlpool",
      "actions": 2,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "primal",
        "water"
      ],
      "text": "Requirements The drowned mummy is underwater\n\n---\n\nEffect The drowned mummy commands the water to churn, creating a powerful whirlpool centered on itself. Each creature within a 30-foot emanation centered on the drowned mummy takes 14d8 bludgeoning damage (DC 38 basic Reflex save) as the powerful current batters them around. A creature that fails this save is pushed 20 feet away from the mummy and also falls Prone on a critical failure. The drowned mummy can't use Whirlpool again for 1d4 rounds."
    }
  ],
  "text": "Rarely artificially created, drowned mummies are miserable, dripping undead that have adapted to exist in an aquatic environment, usually over centuries, after their tomb or lair becomes flooded."
